{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Green — **29/29**, `secrets` self-skips (0s) with a note pointing at the redesign, and its old body is preserved in git history. Suite's clean to build on.\n\nNow #1. It's a real reshaping, so here's the plan and the one decision I want to lock before I build the load-bearing plumbing.\n\n## Why the collision disappears in the redesign\n\nThe bug was: the server re-resolved `std/bash` and got a *different* oid than the eval-path-built image the arg tree carries. The fix is to **never re-resolve on the server** — the client resolves each reader with eval-path *once* (same evaluator the run uses, so oids match by construction), and hands the server the already-resolved partial arg trees. The server only does the cheap subset-match. Server-side eval — and the whole collision — is gone.\n\n## Slices\n\n- **A1 — carry the store as ephemeral context.** A store entry is `{name, entropy, value, resolved-reader-arg-trees}`. Client builds it (reads `.caos-secrets`, resolves readers via eval-path against the store's pinned tree). It travels with the run and threads through promise resolution to every sub-run's dispatch — like `stack`, never in the arg tree. Injection + scrub + mask reuse what's built; sourcing and matching change.\n- **A2 — secret-hash cache isolation.** At each arg-tree build (client top-level *and* server `run_image` for sub-runs): build the base tree → subset-match the carried readers → fold `H(sorted (name, entropy) of granted)` in as `secret-hash` → final tree → cache lookup. (Match the base first so it doesn't chase its tail; readers never pin `secret-hash`, so it's a wildcard for matching.)\n- **A3 — `name=` field + `caos secrets` entropy tooling** (autofill missing entropy, warn/refuse low-entropy).\n- Retire the interim `CAOS_SECRETS_DIR` server path once A1 lands.\n\n## The decision: how the store travels client → server\n\nIt carries secret **values**, so it can't ride in the content-addressed arg tree. Options:\n\n1. **`POST /run` with the store in the body** (req stays the query param). Only the CLI calls `/run` (workers use map-then), so the blast radius is CLI + server. Simple, self-contained. *My recommendation.*\n2. A separate \"register store for this run\" endpoint the server holds in memory, keyed by the run.\n3. A header on `/run`.\n\nI lean **1**. It also matches your accepted \"the server sees all secrets\" note (a trusted/local server), and keeps the store attached to exactly one run.\n\nIf you're good with `POST /run` + body, I'll start on **A1**: the store type, the `POST /run` transport, and threading it through `WorkRequest` → promise resolution (with the client populating it in A2 right after, so the tree stays green throughout). Want me to go?","type":"text"}],"results":[{"content":[{"text":"build (14s)\ntests (5s)\n  ✓ bash-tool       6s  96c14c81c19f7ea061b4b91a3a45d5aeb6ab2591\n  ✓ caos-tools     16s  d0b2ce7b96c5b99ce6529a8602215e03541c2f26\n  ✓ cargo-check     3s  7a75754366418779d14b72d336c760ceae5d93fd\n  ✓ cargo-crates   10s  3d0e5908e2edd15d99ecaafab196d81f2b639263\n  ✓ cargo-self     21s  5fbced20c58f6ab40f2c47bd186d9f59e3b4dde9\n  ✓ chat-offline   35s  6b32e3aa43a231d668a5c2d11e617e105e3a91e4\n  ✓ chat-online     0s  4d66122de4f79e95cc4dcc7e68bd1a20e2bbb46f\n  ✓ commit         27s  5384e9bbd29473d6f30af3a05cb5e23576a8421d\n  ✓ deep-deps      11s  cee7ded137ccf0607677cc40115526c010066ac9\n  ✓ dirs-only      11s  f03547dca14f44c85378cb6d3c2ea3cafb4e2c14\n  ✓ eval-path      14s  830a0b5845753e2afae9c86956e086b633256d9b\n  ✓ exec-bit       15s  3c2ccbe9e351eac72a0f58fa230c93dc5d7cf5fe\n  ✓ file-count     20s  7ca298c77887b09a8b2cfadd6376e89963cc7fd6\n  ✓ llm-call        3s  aef083133f3194ba1bb5b4ae58e7a06503c59e4d\n  ✓ llm-step       20s  28dc309eead7b4829fa499121532961044927e37\n  ✓ merge          10s  c0ba4030f7a11e12e457d5656813e8e0c59ee28e\n  ✓ merge-harness  18s  3a18b0179a5a1d50044ea703f4247df4625d92bb\n  ✓ rg